    {
      "slug": "reddit-landlord-notary-clause-backfire",
      "script": "He enforced what clause? My landlord refused to fix a dead furnace in January, then cited an obscure lease clause: every tenant message had to be hand-delivered and notarized. The heat, apparently, needed paperwork. Fine. I found a notary two blocks away, got the demand stamped, then hand-delivered it to his office with a witness present. The same clause gave him twenty-four hours; after that, I could hire an emergency HVAC company and deduct the full cost from rent. He missed the deadline. I paid eleven hundred dollars, sent the notarized invoice, and reduced the following rent payment by that exact amount. He tried filing for eviction. The judge read his favorite clause, dismissed the case in about four minutes, and ordered him to cover my legal filing fees too. Was the landlord's notarized clause worth it?",
      "editor_note": "Punched up to a four-word question hook, compressed the lease mechanics, added one dry paperwork aside, and landed on the landlord's own notarized clause while preserving every claim and shot phrase."
    },
    {
      "slug": "reddit-bakery-empty-box-refund",
      "script": "She returned how much cake? A woman stormed to my bakery counter waving a nearly empty cake box and demanding a full refund because it tasted wrong. Her toddler had blue frosting smeared across his face. The evidence was subtle. Our return policy, taped right there on the counter, refunds custom orders only if at least eighty percent comes back for inspection. I opened the box and counted maybe two slices left inside. Asked where the rest went, she said the kids ate it before she noticed the sign. I photographed the mostly empty box, pointed to the laminated policy sign, and offered to refund the missing eighty percent she could still produce. She grabbed it, threatened a review, and left without the refund or the rest of the cake. Where did the rest of the cake go?",
      "editor_note": "Punched up to a five-word question hook, tightened the empty-box escalation, added one dry evidence aside, and landed on the missing cake while preserving every claim and shot phrase."
    }
